<title>EGYPT: Egyptian March yr/yr inflation down at 5.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Egyptian March yr/yr inflation down at 5.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's consumer price index rose to 5.5 percent year-on-year in March, from 5.4 percent in February, but fell from 6.7 percent in March 1996, the government statistics office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The statistics showed the index for urban areas, set at a base of 100 in the financial year 1986/87, rose 0.6 percent in March 1997 to 378.7 from 376.6 in February 1997.</p>
<p>The index was 358.8 in March 1996.</p>
<p>					 March 1997  Feb 1997  March 1996</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		   +0.6	 +0.2	 +0.4</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		     +5.5	 +5.4	 +6.7</p>
<p>    INDEX  (base 1986/7)	   378.7	 376.6	358.8</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/</p>
